  "source_excerpts": {
    "title": "Certified homogenizing-variable torsion removal as a solving strategy",
    "mechanism": "Object: a bounded h-torsion submodule with certificates h^k*f in the homogeneous ideal. Operation set Sigma: derive a certified torsion element, dehomogenize it, and add the resulting affine consequence. Trichotomy: coordinate-dependent; this is a solver/representation object, not a lossy quotient under the full group translation action. Discarded information: the affine solver discards the h-torsion history; multiplier witnesses preserve its correctness and are fully charged. For homogenized generators F^h, seek low-degree f with h^k f in (F^h). Only add f at h=1 after checking the identity at construction degree E. Separate the desired output degree D, saturation power k, and the largest degree E needed to find and verify the witness. The full saturation is not presumed cheap or even necessary; a small useful submodule could accelerate solving.",
    "minimal_test": {
      "design": "Prime-field digit systems m=2,3,s=3..5 and a separate Boolean n=12 arm; construction E<=8 initially. Exact generating-set identities and independent root checks precede comparisons.",
      "execution_status": "design_only_not_approved",
      "controls": [
        {
          "kind": "baseline",
          "design": "k=0 and no additional generators reproduces plain homogenized/affine solving."
        },
        {
          "kind": "matched_null",
          "design": "Same support and solution count with coefficients randomized; treat fields separately."
        },
        {
          "kind": "known_false",
          "design": "An h-torsion element supported entirely at infinity whose dehomogenization is zero gives no useful fall and must not count as pruning."
        },
        {
          "kind": "identity",
          "design": "Use the stated baseline slice with identical inputs, ordering and certificate policy; output identities must match exactly."
        },
        {
          "kind": "generic_group",
          "design": "For any claimed group information gain, repeat the statistic on relabelled Z/NZ with the same incidence and acquisition budget. Algebra-only comparisons explicitly do not claim a generic-group escape."
        }
      ],
      "required_metrics": [
        "D,k,E, nonzero surviving consequences, solver matrix sizes and total work",
        "all setup, acquisition, unsuccessful-attempt, transport, certificate and verification costs",
        "peak resident memory and total stored bytes",
        "SAT and UNSAT costs separately, or successful and failed incidence attempts separately",
        "loss L=log2(number of represented preimages) and branching b=max verified successors at each retained synopsis; witness storage separately"
      ],
      "budget": {
        "proposed_only": true,
        "maximum_runs": 0,
        "note": "This handoff approves zero runs. A successor needs a new frozen per-cell budget; planning allowance 3 implementation-days and up to 4 CPU-hours/32 GiB for first complete toy cell, scaled only by Coordinator approval. Exhaustive synthetic calibrators may warrant smaller documented bounds."
      },
      "stopping_rules": [
        "Stop on first soundness/completeness control failure and classify the instrument invalid.",
        "At a frozen resource cap report failed_infrastructure without a mathematical verdict.",
        "If valid completed cells miss the quantitative threshold, reject only this mechanism/parameter claim and retain the measured obstruction."
      ],
      "required_artifacts": [
        "frozen source formula/curve/base and seeds",
        "all candidate descriptions and failed attempts",
        "exact control and solution certificates",
        "stage-cost and memory records",
        "independent checker source binding",
        "unpooled raw metrics"
      ]
    },
    "falsification_conditions": [
      "Any valid completed cell exhibits the known-false failure: An h-torsion element supported entirely at infinity whose dehomogenization is zero gives no useful fall and must not count as pruning.",
      "The completed controlled ladder fails the proposed effect: V_new<=0.75 V_plain and total work <=0.8 plain at identical solution count",
      "The charged saving disappears after including construction, canonicalization, failed attempts, memory or recovery.",
      "A purported synopsis merges the collision pair without retaining its distinction: Same torsion dimension with different images after h=1 must lead to different utility counts."
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      "Public generated mathematical instances only, with frozen field, subgroup, curve, factor-base definition, presentation, solver and sample law.",
      "F2 factor-base decomposition is a component, not the proposed new object; the added object is a bounded h-torsion submodule with certificates h^k*f in the homogeneous ideal. F1 generic search is a comparator; any F7 caching/preprocessing is fully charged.",
      "All identity, soundness and completeness certificates must be independently checked before measuring cost.",
      "Prime-field digit/implicit membership is a high-degree or implicit-description escape class of KN-OPEN-020, not a bounded-degree plane-locus exemption. Binary arms use actual Weil descent and never transfer Boolean identities to F_p."
    ],
    "proof_search_map": {
      "bottleneck": "The exact load-bearing step is producing and using a bounded h-torsion submodule with certificates h^k*f in the homogeneous ideal cheaply enough for: V_new<=0.75 V_plain and total work <=0.8 plain at identical solution count",
      "baseline_embedding": {
        "parameter_slice": "k=0 and no additional generators reproduces plain homogenized/affine solving.",
        "reproduction_check": "First prove this equality symbolically; in a successor compare every output/certificate at the smallest exhaustive fixture. No reproduction was executed in this task."
      },
      "observation_collision": {
        "observable": "a bounded h-torsion submodule with certificates h^k*f in the homogeneous ideal",
        "distinct_preimage_search": "Same torsion dimension with different images after h=1 must lead to different utility counts."
      },
      "constructive_transforms": [
        {
          "transform": "representation_reduction",
          "proposed_object": "a bounded h-torsion submodule with certificates h^k*f in the homogeneous ideal",
          "predicted_gain": "V_new<=0.75 V_plain and total work <=0.8 plain at identical solution count"
        }
      ],
      "quantifier_order": "For every admitted public instance in the frozen parameter family, construct certificates with soundness and completeness; for the preregistered distribution and selected fixed design, H1 predicts V_new<=0.75 V_plain and total work <=0.8 plain at identical solution count. Selection may depend on public parameters and charged calibration, never on hidden scalar labels or evaluation outcomes.",
      "method_ceiling": {
        "strongest_certifiable_claim": "A bounded selected torsion family can decrease the maximum matrix size of affine solving by >=25%, after paying its own full-column construction and witness cost. No inference from low-degree torsion dimension alone is valid. A successful finite test is scoped evidence only; a uniform asymptotic theorem requires a separate bound on every growth parameter.",
        "nearby_object_control": "An h-torsion element supported entirely at infinity whose dehomogenization is zero gives no useful fall and must not count as pruning."
      },
      "proof_obligations": [
        {
          "responsibility": "baseline",
          "claim": "k=0 and no additional generators reproduces plain homogenized/affine solving."
        },
        {
          "responsibility": "correctness",
          "claim": "Prove that derive a certified torsion element, dehomogenize it, and add the resulting affine consequence preserves precisely the asserted solution/row/certificate property, with exact witnesses."
        },
        {
          "responsibility": "interface",
          "claim": "Prove recovery after the declared loss: the affine solver discards the h-torsion history; multiplier witnesses preserve its correctness and are fully charged; independently verify every final group relation."
        },
        {
          "responsibility": "size",
          "claim": "Bound all retained data for a bounded h-torsion submodule with certificates h^k*f in the homogeneous ideal including D,k,E, nonzero surviving consequences, solver matrix sizes and total work and certificate storage."
        },
        {
          "responsibility": "runtime",
          "claim": "Derive and charge the entire expression: C_torsion(E)+C_identity_verify+LA(V_new)+C_solution_verify; M=full construction matrix plus torsion witnesses and solver workspace; data=all candidates, including those vanishing on dehomogenization."
        },
        {
          "responsibility": "success_probability",
          "claim": "At E<=8 there is a nonzero surviving torsion family whose solver savings exceed its construction cost on >=half the fixed toy instances. Establish or test this separately from runtime and correctness."
        },
        {
          "responsibility": "strictness",
          "claim": "Exhibit completed controlled evidence or a theorem for V_new<=0.75 V_plain and total work <=0.8 plain at identical solution count; equal solution count or low output degree alone does not establish it."
        }
      ],
      "not_applicable_reason": null
    },
    "interpretation_limits": [
      "Proposals only: no experiment, proof validation, asymptotic improvement, verified novelty, hypothesis transition or goal completion.",
      "All cost inequalities are targets or conditional algebraic accounting, not measurements. Matched Pollard rho O(N^(1/2)) group operations, small memory; BSGS O(N^(1/2)) time and memory. These generic reference rows do not establish that the proposed method wins.",
      "R3 labels the attacked representation stage, not a new group law. Loss or branching must be certified against Sigma; no full-translation quotient claim.",
      "Degree, reduced-basis size, rank deficit, first fall and actual solving work are distinct. The known shared S_4 defect record must be audited before reusing any old implementation.",
      "Negative evidence would concern the exact tested representation, operations, domain and budget-independent completed cells only."
    ],
